+Controller Certification Playbook (torque-level & whole-body)
+
+Overview
+- Purpose: step-by-step plan to take controller code from prototype -> certifiable deliverable.
+- Intended audience: controls engineers, safety engineers, test engineers.
+
+Steps
+1. HARA & Requirements
+  - Fill ops/robotics/certification/hara_template.csv with robot-specific hazards.
+  - Derive requirements (timing, force limits, detection thresholds) and record in test_matrix.csv.
+
+2. Controller Hardening
+  - Implement watchdog, bounds, saturation, and monotonicity checks (use torque_controller_watchdog).
+  - Add traces: all commanded/actual torques, timestamps, estimator states at controller frequency.
+
+3. Formal Modeling
+  - Produce TLA+ or model-checker spec of controller invariants (see ops/formal/*).
+  - Run Apalache/TLC and resolve counterexamples.
+
+4. HIL Test Suite
+  - Create deterministic HIL scenarios: trajectory_following, contact_injection, sensor_dropout.
+  - Use waveform capture & compare (ops/robotics/control/validation) and define acceptance (MSE thresholds).
+
+5. Performance SLOs
+  - Validate RT loop jitter, safe-stop latency, and servo latency on representative hardware. Use orchestrate_rt_full.sh.
+
+6. Evidence Packaging
+  - Package HIL logs, formal proofs, signed controller binaries, and MLflow runs.
+  - Sign the package with cosign (KMS) and register in Rekor.
+
+7. Third-party Review
+  - Submit package to certifier; iterate on findings and re-run HIL.
+
+Artifacts to deliver
+- HARA spreadsheet, test matrix, TLA+ specs & Apalache outputs, HIL bundles (signed), controller source & binaries, MLflow runs, cosign/Rekor evidence.
